# Employee Management System

## Overview

Employee Management System built using Node.js, Express.js, and PostgreSQL.

The project provides Employee Management APIs with Authentication, Authorization, Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), Employee Management Operations, and Dashboard Analytics.

---

## Features

### Authentication

* User Registration
* User Login
* JWT Authentication
* bcrypt Password Hashing

### Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

Supported Roles:

* ADMIN
* MANAGER
* EMPLOYEE

#### Admin Permissions

* Create Employee
* Update Employee
* Delete Employee
* View All Employees

#### Manager Permissions

* View Employees Within Their Department

#### Employee Permissions

* View Own Profile

---

## Employee Features

* Create Employee
* Get Employee By ID
* Get All Employees
* Update Employee
* Soft Delete Employee
* Search Employees
* Filter Employees By Department
* Sort Employees By Salary
* Sort Employees By Created Date
* View Active Employees
* Pagination

---

## Dashboard Analytics

### Employee Overview

* Total Employees
* Active Employees
* Inactive Employees

### Department Analytics

* Employee Count by Department
* Active Employees by Department

### Salary Analytics

* Total Salary
* Average Salary
* Highest Salary
* Lowest Salary

### Employee Joining Trends

* Month-wise Employee Onboarding Statistics

### Dashboard Endpoint

GET /api/dashboard

Returns all dashboard metrics in a single response.

---

## Tech Stack

* Node.js
* Express.js
* PostgreSQL
* pg
* JWT
* bcrypt
* dotenv

---

## Database Design

### Departments

| Column | Type         |
| ------ | ------------ |
| id     | UUID         |
| name   | VARCHAR(100) |

### Employees

| Column        | Type          |
| ------------- | ------------- |
| id            | UUID          |
| first_name    | VARCHAR(100)  |
| last_name     | VARCHAR(100)  |
| email         | VARCHAR(200)  |
| department_id | UUID          |
| salary        | DECIMAL(10,2) |
| is_active     | BOOLEAN       |
| created_at    | TIMESTAMP     |
| updated_at    | TIMESTAMP     |

### Users

| Column      | Type         |
| ----------- | ------------ |
| id          | UUID         |
| email       | VARCHAR(200) |
| password    | VARCHAR(255) |
| role        | VARCHAR(20)  |
| employee_id | UUID         |
| created_at  | TIMESTAMP    |

---

## API Endpoints

### Authentication

#### Register

POST /auth/register

#### Login

POST /auth/login

---

### Employee APIs

#### Get All Employees

GET /employees

#### Get Employee By ID

GET /employees/:id

#### Create Employee

POST /employees

#### Update Employee

PUT /employees/:id

#### Soft Delete Employee

DELETE /employees/:id

#### Active Employees

GET /employees/active

#### Search Employees

GET /employees/search

#### Filter By Department

GET /employees/department

#### Sort By Salary

GET /employees/salary

#### Sort By Date

GET /employees/date

#### Employee Profile

GET /employees/me

#### Department Members

GET /employees/department-members

---

### Dashboard Analytics

#### Get Dashboard Metrics

GET /api/dashboard

Returns:

* Employee Overview
* Department Analytics
* Salary Analytics
* Employee Joining Trends

---

## Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file:

```env
PORT=3000

DB_USER=your_db_user
DB_PASSWORD=your_db_password
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=your_db_name

JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key
```

---

## Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone <repository-url>
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

---

## Run Project

Development Mode:

```bash
npm run dev
```

Production Mode:

```bash
npm start
```

